# oracle: cut-down examples/mliap/in.mliap.snap.chem (2x2x2 cells instead of 4x4x4, 20 steps): hybrid/overlay zbl + mliap model linear with descriptor sna chemflag 1 (InP_JCPA2020), nve, velocities from atom-style variables (the engine velocity create uses its own RNG), thermo every 10 steps
# oracle-potentials: InP_JCPA2020.mliap InP_JCPA2020.mliap.model InP_JCPA2020.mliap.descriptor InP_JCPA2020.snapcoeff InP_JCPA2020.snapparam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12 skip=press
# press is skipped: measured with native LAMMPS (black box), the virial of this chem cell differs from the engine by about 2e-4 bar (6e-10 relative, the same offset as pair snap chemflag 1 without velocities), and this cut-down cell has |P| of about 315 bar, so the 1e-9 relative test cannot hold; pe, forces and positions are compared
units           metal
variable nsteps index 20
variable nrep equal 2
variable a equal 5.83
boundary        p p p
lattice         diamond $a
region          box block 0 ${nrep} 0 ${nrep} 0 ${nrep}
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box basis 5 2 basis 6 2 basis 7 2 basis 8 2
mass 1 114.76
mass 2 30.98
include InP_JCPA2020.mliap
thermo          10
thermo_style custom step pe press
thermo_modify norm yes
thermo_modify format float %.15g
timestep 0.5e-3
neighbor 1.0 bin
neigh_modify once no every 1 delay 0 check yes
variable vx atom 0.02*sin(id)
variable vy atom 0.02*cos(2*id)
variable vz atom 0.02*sin(3*id)
velocity all set v_vx v_vy v_vz
fix 1 all nve
run             ${nsteps}
